#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Introduction {#1-introduction}"
msgstr "1. Wprowadzenie {#1-introduction}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bits, gates, and circuits are the basic building blocks of quantum computing. You will learn quantum computation with the circuit model using quantum bits and gates, and also review the superposition, measurement, and entanglement.\n"
msgstr "Bity, bramki i obwody to podstawowe elementy składowe obliczeń kwantowych. Nauczysz się obliczeń kwantowych z modelem obwodów za pomocą kubitów i bramek kwantowych, a także powtórzysz zasady superpozycji, pomiaru i splątania.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this lesson you will learn:\n"
"- Single-qubit gates\n"
"- Bloch sphere\n"
"- Superposition\n"
"- Measurement\n"
"- Two-qubit gates and entanglement state\n"
msgstr ""
"W tej lekcji dowiesz się o:\n"
"- Bramkach jednoQubitowych\n"
"- Sferze Blocha\n"
"- Superpozycji\n"
"- Pomiarze\n"
"- Bramkach dwuQubitowych i stanie splątania\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At the end of this lecture, you will learn about circuit depth, which is essential for utility-scale quantum computing.\n"
msgstr "Na końcu tego wykładu poznasz pojęcie głębokości obwodu, która jest kluczowa dla obliczeń kwantowych w skali użytkowej.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Computation as a diagram {#2-computation-as-a-diagram}"
msgstr "2. Obliczenia jako diagram {#2-computation-as-a-diagram}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When using qubits or bits, we need to manipulate them in order to turn the inputs we have into the outputs we need. For the simplest programs with very few bits, it is useful to represent this process in a diagram known as a *circuit diagram*.\n"
msgstr "Gdy używamy kubitów lub bitów, musimy nimi manipulować, aby przekształcić dane wejściowe w potrzebne wyniki. W przypadku najprostszych programów z bardzo małą liczbą bitów przydatne jest przedstawienie tego procesu w formie diagramu zwanego *diagramem obwodu*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The bottom-left figure is an example of a classical circuit, and the bottom-right figure is an example of a quantum circuit. In both cases, the inputs are on the left and the outputs are on the right, while the operations are represented by symbols. The symbols used for the operations are called “gates”, mostly for historical reasons.\n"
msgstr "Rysunek w lewym dolnym rogu to przykład obwodu klasycznego, a rysunek w prawym dolnym rogu to przykład obwodu kwantowego. W obu przypadkach dane wejściowe znajdują się po lewej stronie, a wyjściowe po prawej, natomiast operacje są reprezentowane przez symbole. Symbole używane dla operacji nazywane są „bramkami\" — głównie z przyczyn historycznych.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![\"classical logic and quantum circuit\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/classical-vs-quantum.avif)\n"
msgstr "![\"classical logic and quantum circuit\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/classical-vs-quantum.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Single-qubit quantum gate {#3-single-qubit-quantum-gate}"
msgstr "3. Jednokubitowa bramka kwantowa {#3-single-qubit-quantum-gate}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.1 Quantum state and Bloch sphere {#31-quantum-state-and-bloch-sphere}"
msgstr "3.1 Stan kwantowy i sfera Blocha {#31-quantum-state-and-bloch-sphere}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A qubit's state is represented as a superposition of $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$. An arbitrary quantum state is represented as\n"
msgstr "Stan Qubitu jest reprezentowany jako superpozycja $|0\\rangle$ i $|1\\rangle$. Dowolny stan kwantowy jest reprezentowany jako\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle =\\alpha|0\\rangle+ \\beta|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle =\\alpha|0\\rangle+ \\beta|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are complex numbers such that $|\\alpha|^2+|\\beta|^2=1$.\n"
msgstr "gdzie $\\alpha$ i $\\beta$ są liczbami zespolonymi takimi, że $|\\alpha|^2+|\\beta|^2=1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$ are vectors in the two-dimensional complex vector space:\n"
msgstr "$|0\\rangle$ i $|1\\rangle$ są wektorami w dwuwymiarowej zespolonej przestrzeni wektorowej:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"|1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0\\\\1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"|1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0\\\\1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Therefore, an arbitrary quantum state is also represented as\n"
msgstr "Dlatego dowolny stan kwantowy jest również reprezentowany jako\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\alpha\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} + \\beta\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\alpha\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} + \\beta\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "From this, we can see that the state of a quantum bit is a unit vector in a two-dimensional complex inner product space with an orthonormal basis of $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$. It is normalized to 1.\n"
msgstr "Z tego wynika, że stan bitu kwantowego jest wektorem jednostkowym w dwuwymiarowej zespolonej przestrzeni z iloczynem wewnętrznym, z ortonormalną bazą $|0\\rangle$ i $|1\\rangle$. Jest znormalizowany do 1.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\psi|\\psi\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha^* & \\beta^*\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\\n"
"\\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = 1\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\psi|\\psi\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha^* & \\beta^*\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\\n"
"\\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = 1\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ |\\psi\\rangle =\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}$ is also called the statevector.\n"
msgstr ""
"$ |\\psi\\rangle =\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}$ jest również nazywany wektorem stanu (statevector).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A single-qubit quantum state is also represented as\n"
msgstr "Jednokubitowy stan kwantowy jest również reprezentowany jako\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"=\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}|0\\rangle+e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}|1\\rangle\n"
"=\\left( \\begin{pmatrix} \\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\\\ e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"=\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}|0\\rangle+e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}|1\\rangle\n"
"=\\left( \\begin{pmatrix} \\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\\\ e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $\\theta$ and $\\varphi$ are the angles of the Bloch sphere in the following figure.\n"
msgstr "gdzie $\\theta$ i $\\varphi$ są kątami sfery Blocha przedstawionej na poniższym rysunku.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Bloch sphere](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/bloch.avif)\n"
"In the next few code cells, we will build up basic calculations from constituent pieces in Qiskit. We'll construct an empty circuit and then add quantum operations, discussing the gates and visualizing their effects as we go.\n"
"You can run the cell by \"Shift\" + \"Enter\". Import the libraries first.\n"
msgstr ""
"![Bloch sphere](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/bloch.avif)\n"
"W kolejnych kilku komórkach kodu zbudujemy podstawowe obliczenia z elementów składowych w Qiskit. Skonstruujemy pusty Circuit, a następnie będziemy dodawać operacje kwantowe, omawiając bramki i wizualizując ich efekty w miarę postępu.\n"
"Możesz uruchomić komórkę za pomocą \"Shift\" + \"Enter\". Najpierw zaimportuj biblioteki.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the quantum circuit {#prepare-the-quantum-circuit}"
msgstr "Przygotowanie Circuit kwantowego {#prepare-the-quantum-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will create and draw a single-qubit circuit.\n"
msgstr "Stworzymy i narysujemy jednokubitowy Circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/fdef9137-9e39-4b05-afa9-9091766053f6-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/fdef9137-9e39-4b05-afa9-9091766053f6-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "X gate {#x-gate}"
msgstr "Gate X {#x-gate}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The X gate is a $\\pi$ rotation around the $x$ axis of the Bloch sphere.\n"
"Applying the X gate to $|0\\rangle$ results in $|1\\rangle$, and applying the X gate to $|1\\rangle$ results in $|0\\rangle$, so it is an operation similar to the classical NOT gate, and is also known as bit flip. The matrix representation of the X gate is below.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gate X to obrót o $\\pi$ wokół osi $x$ sfery Blocha.\n"
"Zastosowanie Gate X do $|0\\rangle$ daje $|1\\rangle$, a zastosowanie Gate X do $|1\\rangle$ daje $|0\\rangle$, więc jest to operacja podobna do klasycznej bramki NOT i znana jest również jako przerzut bitu. Macierzowa reprezentacja Gate X jest poniżej.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"X = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"X = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/b3468430-0cbc-44ab-bd21-901436662a4b-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/b3468430-0cbc-44ab-bd21-901436662a4b-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In IBM Quantum&reg;, the initial state is set to $|0\\rangle$, so the quantum circuit above in matrix representation is\n"
msgstr "W IBM Quantum&reg; stan początkowy jest ustawiony na $|0\\rangle$, więc powyższy Circuit kwantowy w reprezentacji macierzowej ma postać\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"X|0\\rangle=  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\ 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = |1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"X|0\\rangle=  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\ 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = |1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, let's run this circuit using a statevector simulator.\n"
msgstr "Następnie uruchommy ten obwód przy użyciu symulatora wektora stanu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/efb727e8-f51e-4903-aa0f-e4c099316815-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/efb727e8-f51e-4903-aa0f-e4c099316815-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Vertical vector is displayed as row vector, with complex numbers (the imaginary part is indexed by $j$ ).\n"
msgstr "Wektor pionowy jest wyświetlany jako wektor wierszowy, z liczbami zespolonymi (część urojona jest indeksowana przez $j$ ).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "H gate {#h-gate}"
msgstr "Gate H {#h-gate}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Hadamard gate is a $\\pi$ rotation around an axis halfway between the $x$ and $z$ axes on the Bloch sphere. Applying the H gate to $|0\\rangle$ creates a superposition state such as $\\frac{|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}$. The matrix representation of the H gate is below.\n"
msgstr "Gate Hadamarda to obrót o $\\pi$ wokół osi leżącej w połowie drogi między osiami $x$ i $z$ na sferze Blocha. Zastosowanie Gate H do $|0\\rangle$ tworzy stan superpozycji taki jak $\\frac{|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}$. Macierzowa reprezentacja Gate H jest poniżej.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/574c35f0-26a9-423a-8d65-7140ba7398e3-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/574c35f0-26a9-423a-8d65-7140ba7398e3-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/7adf0e93-6db3-4aa8-800f-c91c8cc46001-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/7adf0e93-6db3-4aa8-800f-c91c8cc46001-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is\n"
"$$\n"
"H|0\\rangle= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.707 \\\\\n"
"0.707\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"To jest\n"
"$$\n"
"H|0\\rangle= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.707 \\\\\n"
"0.707\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This superposition state is so common and important, that it is given its own symbol:\n"
msgstr "Ten stan superpozycji jest tak powszechny i ważny, że otrzymał własny symbol:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|+\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|+\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By applying the $H$ gate on the $|0\\rangle$, we created a superposition of $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$ where measurement in the computational basis (along z in the Bloch sphere picture) would give you each state with equal probabilities.\n"
msgstr "Stosując Gate $H$ na $|0\\rangle$, stworzyliśmy superpozycję $|0\\rangle$ i $|1\\rangle$, gdzie pomiar w bazie obliczeniowej (wzdłuż osi z na sferze Blocha) dałby każdy stan z równym prawdopodobieństwem.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "$|-\\rangle$ state {#rangle-state}"
msgstr "Stan $|-\\rangle$ {#rangle-state}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You might have guessed that there is a corresponding  $|-\\rangle$ state:\n"
"$$\n"
"|-\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{|0\\rangle -|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"$$\n"
"To create this state, first apply an X gate to make $|1\\rangle$, then apply an H gate.\n"
msgstr ""
"Być może zgadłeś, że istnieje odpowiadający stan $|-\\rangle$:\n"
"$$\n"
"|-\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{|0\\rangle -|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Aby stworzyć ten stan, najpierw zastosuj Gate X, aby uzyskać $|1\\rangle$, a następnie zastosuj Gate H.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/b8e96fc4-6708-415e-b8fc-ac69eaeae750-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/b8e96fc4-6708-415e-b8fc-ac69eaeae750-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/f42b82aa-7a15-4f81-8530-b997d4c6e0de-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/f42b82aa-7a15-4f81-8530-b997d4c6e0de-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is\n"
msgstr "To jest\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H|1\\rangle= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\\\n"
"1 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\\\n"
"-1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.707 \\\\\\\n"
"-0.707\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle) = |-\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H|1\\rangle= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\\\n"
"1 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\\\n"
"-1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.707 \\\\\\\n"
"-0.707\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle) = |-\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying the $H$ gate on $|1\\rangle$ results in an equal superposition of $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$, but the sign of $|1\\rangle$ is negative.\n"
msgstr "Zastosowanie Gate $H$ na $|1\\rangle$ daje równą superpozycję $|0\\rangle$ i $|1\\rangle$, ale znak przy $|1\\rangle$ jest ujemny.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.2 Single-qubit quantum state and unitary evolution {#32-single-qubit-quantum-state-and-unitary-evolution}"
msgstr "3.2 Stan kwantowy pojedynczego qubit i ewolucja unitarna {#32-single-qubit-quantum-state-and-unitary-evolution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The actions of all the gates we have seen so far have been *unitary*, which means they can be represented by a unitary operator. In other words, the output state can be obtained by acting on the initial state with a unitary matrix:\n"
msgstr "Działanie wszystkich bramek, które do tej pory poznaliśmy, jest *unitarne*, co oznacza, że można je opisać operatorem unitarnym. Innymi słowy, stan wyjściowy otrzymujemy, działając na stan początkowy macierzą unitarną:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi^{'}\\rangle = U|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi^{'}\\rangle = U|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A unitary matrix is a matrix satisfying\n"
msgstr "Macierz unitarna to macierz spełniająca warunek\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger}U =U U^{\\dagger} = I.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger}U =U U^{\\dagger} = I.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In terms of quantum computer operation, we would say that applying a quantum gate to the qubit evolves the quantum state. Common single-qubit gates include the following.\n"
msgstr "Jeśli chodzi o działanie komputera kwantowego, powiemy, że zastosowanie Gate'u kwantowego do qubit ewoluuje stan kwantowy. Do typowych Gate'ów jednoQubitowych należą poniższe.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli gates:\n"
msgstr "Bramki Pauliego:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"X = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= |0\\rangle \\langle 1|+|1\\rangle \\langle 0|\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"X = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= |0\\rangle \\langle 1|+|1\\rangle \\langle 0|\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Y = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & -i \\\\\n"
"i & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= -i|0\\rangle \\langle 1|+i|1\\rangle \\langle 0|\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Y = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & -i \\\\\n"
"i & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= -i|0\\rangle \\langle 1|+i|1\\rangle \\langle 0|\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= |0\\rangle \\langle 0|-|1\\rangle \\langle 1|\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= |0\\rangle \\langle 0|-|1\\rangle \\langle 1|\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the outer product was calculated as follows:\n"
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle \\langle 0|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle \\langle 0|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"gdzie iloczyn zewnętrzny obliczono następująco:\n"
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle \\langle 0|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle \\langle 0|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle \\langle 1|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle \\langle 1|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle \\langle 1|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle \\langle 1|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Other typical single-qubit gates:\n"
"$$\n"
"H= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix},\\quad\n"
"S = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & i \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"T = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & exp(i\\pi/4) \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Inne typowe Gate'y jednoQubitowe:\n"
"$$\n"
"H= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix},\\quad\n"
"S = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & i \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"T = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & exp(i\\pi/4) \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"R_x(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta X/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}X = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} &  -i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"-i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} & cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"R_x(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta X/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}X = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} &  -i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"-i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} & cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"R_y(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta Y/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}Y = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} &  - sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} & cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"R_y(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta Y/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}Y = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} &  - sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} & cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"R_z(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta Z/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}Z = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"e^{-i\\theta /2} &  0 \\\\\n"
"0 & e^{i\\theta /2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"R_z(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta Z/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}Z = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"e^{-i\\theta /2} &  0 \\\\\n"
"0 & e^{i\\theta /2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The meaning and use of these are described in more detail in the [Basics of Quantum Information](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information) course.\n"
msgstr "Znaczenie i zastosowanie tych bramka'ów zostały opisane szczegółowo w kursie [Podstawy informacji kwantowej](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information).\n"

